id: pm-web-p0me
title: "Let operators run their own consent manager: storage-notice switch, replay-private regions, sign-in analytics events"
description: "Operators who run an opt-in consent manager at their reverse proxy see two banners today, and the built-in storage notice claims no optional tracking exists, which is wrong for such deployments. pm-web also renders private project, item and account data that must stay out of session-replay tools by default, and sign-in starts are invisible to analytics."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-web#308",privacy;analytics;consent;operator-config
created_at: "2026-11-09T01:33:28.349Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T06:29:32.290Z"
author: pi-glm
acceptance_criteria: "PM_WEB_STORAGE_NOTICE=on|off server setting (default on) documented in the README configuration table; GET /api/ui-config returns {storageNotice:boolean}; With off, cookie-consent.js never shows the notice, never writes pm_cookie_preferences_v1, and data-cookie-settings buttons fall back to a plain link to the operator's cookie-settings legal page; with on behaviour is unchanged; fetch failure falls back to on without throwing; Every private-content container (#main-app, #modal-container, #toast-container, #live-copy-announcement) and dynamically created private overlays carry data-umami-block; the sign-in screen stays unblocked; a test fails if any listed container loses the attribute; Sign-in buttons carry data-umami-event auth_sign_in_started with provider password / oidc; no user name, e-mail or token in any attribute; privacy-policy.html template tells operators running an analytics or consent manager to describe it and explains PM_WEB_STORAGE_NOTICE=off; no visitor-visible vendor names anywhere; Tests cover both setting values over real HTTP and the client script over the built artifact; focused tests, typecheck and lint pass locally"
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T01:38:44.464Z",pi-glm,"Design: (1) New setting PM_WEB_STORAGE_NOTICE (default on; only the exact value 'off' disables) read per request by src/routes/ui-config.ts and exposed to the classic consent script via a minimal unauthenticated GET /api/ui-config -> {storageNotice:boolean}, mounted on the static-asset rate tier. Reusing /api/auth/oidc/config would not fit: the consent script is a classic script without the SPA api() wrapper, runs on the standalone legal pages too, and that route's shape (enabled,label) is OIDC-specific. (2) public/src/cookie-consent.ts resolves the config first (banner starts hidden, so no flash): with on, behaviour is unchanged; with off the banner never shows, nothing is written to pm_cookie_preferences_v1, and [data-cookie-settings] buttons are replaced by plain links to /cookie-settings (the operator's deployed legal page). Every fetch failure (network, non-OK, unparsable body) falls back to on, and the read never throws. (3) data-umami-block added to #main-app, #modal-container, #toast-container, #live-copy-announcement in index.html, plus self-marking for the dynamically created private overlays (graph context menu, graph tooltip, the two graph dependency modals inserted on body, both offline-recovery notices). Sign-in screen stays unblocked. No widely used vendor-neutral attribute convention was found for replay blocking, so only the tracker's own data-umami-block attribute API is used. (4) Sign-in start events: data-umami-event=auth_sign_in_started with provider password (#auth-submit) and oidc (#oidc-login); no user data in any attribute. (5) privacy-policy.html template gained an 'Analytics and consent management' section (operators must describe any analytics/consent manager, and PM_WEB_STORAGE_NOTICE=off is explained); README configuration table documents the setting. Branding rule kept: the vendor name appears nowhere visitor-visible, only in data-umami-* attribute names."
  "2026-11-09T01:38:49.399Z",pi-glm,"Revert proof (behavioural, in the package worktree, originals restored and re-verified after each): reverting public/index.html to origin/main -> replay-privacy fails ('every private-content container carries data-umami-block' and 'sign-in start buttons'); reverting public/src/cookie-consent.ts to origin/main -> consent-notice fails (off: banner never shows / plain-link fallback / endpoint read, 3 failures, 5 pass); reverting only storageNoticeEnabled in src/routes/ui-config.ts to always return true -> ui-config-routes fails (off over real HTTP + case/whitespace variant + pure function, 3 failures, 5 pass). After restoration all three files pass again."
  "2026-11-09T01:38:50.410Z",pi-glm,"Local gates: focused suites pass (ui-config-routes 8, consent-notice 8, replay-privacy 6, static-scripts 9, legal-pages 6, legal-routes 8, brand-copy/i18n/brand-assets/package-metadata/packaging 34 -> 79 total, 0 fail). npm run lint, npm run duplication (0%), npm run docstring, npm run typecheck (server+frontend), npm run build:test all pass. Full release:check (coverage, capacity, pack) is CI's gate; the local test database is not running here."
  "2026-11-09T01:39:48.383Z",pi-glm,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/308 opened from branch feat/operator-consent-integration (single commit a1eba08) with this item linked. Local gates recorded above; full release:check (npm + Bun, coverage/capacity/pack) runs in CI."
  "2026-11-09T05:56:30.070Z",codex-agent,"Continuation: inspected the existing branch, remote head, ready PR 308 and this item; retaining the implementation and unfinished review fixes. Addressing stalled UI-config reads with a bounded fallback covering response bodies, and suppressing password sign-in events on the registration tab. Will verify behavioral reverts in a disposable copy, run local gates, and update the same PR without touching review threads."
  "2026-11-09T06:01:35.231Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in a disposable non-git copy (the package worktree was not mutated): fixed HTTP tests pass 8/8 without git. Removing the config deadline produces 3 failures in consent-notice (10 pass); restoring passes 13/13. Removing only the switchAuthTab event-update call makes the actual login/register/login execution fail (6 pass, 1 fail); restoring passes 7/7. Changing storageNoticeEnabled to always true fails 3 real HTTP/parser cases (5 pass); restoring passes 8/8. Removing data-umami-block from each of main-app, modal-container, toast-container and live-copy-announcement independently fails the private-container test. Reverting sign-in button markup fails its attribute test. All restored markup passes 7/7. The deadline also cancels the stalled request, covers stalled response bodies, clears a completed read timer, and ignores late off responses."
  "2026-11-09T06:02:13.888Z",codex-agent,"Validation: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/ui-config-routes.test.ts test/consent-notice.test.ts test/replay-privacy.test.ts passes 28/28 (HTTP 8, consent 13, replay/sign-in 7), including the actual shared submit-button tab transitions. The same command plus test/static-scripts.test.ts test/legal-pages.test.ts test/legal-routes.test.ts test/brand-copy.test.ts test/i18n.test.ts test/brand-assets.test.ts test/package-metadata.test.ts test/packaging.test.ts passes 85/85, zero failures/skips. npm run typecheck, npm run lint, npm run duplication (0%), npm run docstring and npm run build:test pass. Both npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass their code/build gates then stop at the required database preflight because no throwaway PostgreSQL server is reachable. Full npm/Bun coverage, capacity and packed-consumer acceptance therefore require CI on PR 308. No unrelated services were started."
  "2026-11-09T06:02:15.236Z",codex-agent,"Review handoff for PR 308: PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c61Gkeb is addressed by the bounded whole-read timeout (request and body stalls, cancellation, late response, timer cleanup); its regression tests fail on deadline revert. PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c61Gkec is addressed by removing password sign-in attributes on registration and restoring them on sign-in; the real switchAuthTab execution fails when its event-update call is removed. Review threads remain untouched for orchestrator handling. This item remains in_progress and open for verification; releasing only this agent's claim. No pm CLI/SDK gaps encountered."
  "2026-11-09T06:02:44.086Z",codex-agent,"Additional local health finding: pm health --strict-exit reports extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew:2026.11.2:2026.11.8:pm-github for the pre-existing local extension installation. This is separate from the feature and from the passing focused tests. CI installs the repository-pinned managed extension via scripts/install-pm-github.sh; dependency pins and local managed extensions are left unchanged. No product SDK capability gap was found."
  "2026-11-09T06:29:32.290Z",codex-agent,"Bounded CI handoff for implementation commit a47a12ec98643563bd3f1b0164cf454e5dd9af41: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/42570740852 has a fully successful test (26) job. Its full npm and Bun release gates each pass 912/912 suite tests and 2/2 capacity tests, with zero skipped tests; both coverage gates report all 79 configured source files and thresholds met. CodeQL run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/42570741016 and graph browser run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/42570740902 also pass. The test (22) job remains in its full npm release gate after roughly 26 minutes of CI waiting; its later Bun gate is still pending. Do not treat that matrix as approved. This tracker receipt changes no implementation; fresh exact-head checks for the receipt commit must finish through https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/308/checks. Additional no-git verification passes the UI-config HTTP suite 8/8 in a disposable plain directory with no Git executable available. The item remains open and unclaimed; review threads remain untouched for orchestrator handling."
